IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `csca-college`

-- Civil Service College Act 2001, ss 5(2), 7(2), 9, 13(3), 14(1)(d), 16, 18, 32(4), 33, 38-41 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_civil-service-college-act-2001.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a former employee leaking a participant's assessment` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS TRUE
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`an officer disclosing in the course of duties` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS TRUE
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS TRUE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`an employee giving evidence under a court order` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS TRUE
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS TRUE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`a participant repeating what a lecturer said` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS FALSE
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`a member disclosing what he learned outside his duties` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

§ `s 38 -- symbol`

